# nl-startup-3: daemon memory telemetry and the stall sampler

[lib.rs]
After `pub mod daemon_log;` add:
    pub mod telemetry;

[composition]
Where the daemon is composed (the place that builds `DaemonLog` and the `Lifecycle`/session directory, run by serving), build once and spawn:

    let telemetry = telemetry::Telemetry::new(
        telemetry::Seams {
            work: Arc::new(move || WorkCounts { /* active_calls: transport active + queued split, model-proxy bridge active;
                                                   queued_calls: transport queued; busy_sessions: session directory busy count;
                                                   busy_memory_agents: agent dispatch broker in-flight (memory_agent_watch) */ }),
            memory: Arc::new(telemetry::process_memory),
            log: log.line_log(),                       // daemon.log "[daemon] <line>"
            now_ms: Arc::new(daemon_log::system_now_ms),
            pid: std::process::id(),
        },
        Arc::new(telemetry::DiskProfileStore::new(data_dir.clone())),
        data_dir.join("profiles"),
        tokens.maintenance_io,
        run_cancel.clone(),
        Arc::new(|| serde_json::Value::Null),          // or Executors::diagnostics() as JSON: kept in a lag profile's "state"
    );
    tokio::spawn(telemetry.clone().run(run_cancel.clone()));

and call `telemetry.note_activity()` where Node called `noteDaemonActivity()` (start and settle of every call on both front doors:
the `reportingIdleActivity` wrapper), next to the idle-GC activity mark if the Rust side has one.

[crash_record.rs]
`crash_record::memory()` is the same read as `telemetry::process_memory()`; make it call
`let m = telemetry::process_memory(); (m.rss_bytes, m.heap_bytes)` and delete its two cfg copies (crash_record.rs is not this task's file).

[compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING]
No protocol method is added: nothing to remove.
